<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>International news from the Americas - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage of the political, social and economic issues in the United States, Canada, Mexico, Argentina, Brazil and across the Americas.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/</link><lastBuildDate>Wed, 30 Sep 2026 05:36:33 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Supreme Court lifts restrictions on third-country deportations</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-supreme-court-lifts-restrictions-on-third-country-deportations</link><description>
The US Supreme Court on Tuesday cleared the Trump administration to resume deporting migrants to countries other than their own while it considers the legality of the practice. The court’s conservative majority temporarily blocked safeguards requiring deportees to receive notice of where they would be sent and time to raise persecution concerns.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3dfdf88-8270-11f1-9005-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%AD%D9%83%D9%85%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A7-%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B4%D9%86%D8%B7%D9%86.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3dfdf88-8270-11f1-9005-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%AD%D9%83%D9%85%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A7-%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B4%D9%86%D8%B7%D9%86.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">e7dbab8a-bc5b-11f1-b989-8b9c91320d8d</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 23:17:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b3dfdf88-8270-11f1-9005-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D8%AD%D9%83%D9%85%D8%A9-%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B9%D9%84%D9%8A%D8%A7-%D9%88%D8%A7%D8%B4%D9%86%D8%B7%D9%86.jpg">© Elizabeth Frantz, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>OpenAI cancels release of new artificial intelligence model over safety concerns</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-openai-cancels-release-new-ai-model-safety-concerns</link><description>
OpenAI will not release its latest artificial intelligence model, Astra 6.1, after internal tests found it fell short of safety standards, the maker of ChatGPT confirmed on Monday. The decision came ahead of a meeting of AI leaders at the White House Tuesday convened by US President Donald Trump and House Speaker Mike Johnson amid mounting controversy over the risks posed by rogue AI. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24f7f624-bbab-11f1-a10f-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/ed72c19924b58aed5d30c1b4fd404394858653b3.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24f7f624-bbab-11f1-a10f-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/ed72c19924b58aed5d30c1b4fd404394858653b3.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1e04de42-bbae-11f1-a598-37818c4a8cee</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:54:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/24f7f624-bbab-11f1-a10f-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/ed72c19924b58aed5d30c1b4fd404394858653b3.jpg">© Andrej Ivanov, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Argentina’s Milei threatens to sue UK over Falkland Islands oil project</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-argentina-milei-arbitration-falklands-oil-project</link><description>
Argentine President Javier Milei on Monday threatened to sue the UK over the Sea Lion oil project near the disputed Falkland Islands. Argentina claims sovereignty over the British-administered territory, where a 1982 war killed 255 British and 649 Argentine troops. Developers Navitas and Rockhopper say they hold valid British-issued exploration licences.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79cc0530-a84d-11f1-994b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246770000815.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79cc0530-a84d-11f1-994b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246770000815.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5ead5640-bba9-11f1-a8b0-4b0a8e7f93cb</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 02:13:40 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/79cc0530-a84d-11f1-994b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26246770000815.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US prosecutors reopen Cornell university gang rape investigation</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260929-us-prosecutors-cornell-university-gang-rape-investigation</link><description>
US prosecutors reopened an investigation on Monday into an alleged 2024 gang rape at Cornell University after the woman involved accused the school of failing to punish those responsible adequately. In a lawsuit, she said seven Chi Phi fraternity members had drugged her with ketamine and assaulted her.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/763f398e-bb83-11f1-a9d1-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271727531918.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/763f398e-bb83-11f1-a9d1-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271727531918.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">89f0ac00-bb98-11f1-a062-1393ad981d3a</guid><pubDate>Tue, 29 Sep 2026 00:04:48 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/763f398e-bb83-11f1-a9d1-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26271727531918.jpg">© Heather Ainsworth, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US deportations are triggering a 'cascade' of rights abuses, UN experts warn</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260928-us-trump-deportations-triggering-cascade-of-rights-abuses-un-experts-warn-forbidden-stories</link><description>
The Trump administration's policy of deportating thousands of people to countries with which they have no links is "increasing risks of torture and ill-treatment and enforced disappearance", a panel of independent UN experts warned on Monday. An investigation by an international consortium of journalists including FRANCE 24 reporters determined last week that more than 25,000 third-country nationals had been deported by the end of August.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db4a30b2-bb61-11f1-9d45-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25243812139636.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db4a30b2-bb61-11f1-9d45-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25243812139636.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f1028e58-bb5d-11f1-87c5-8ff4b2f5e08d</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 18:01:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/db4a30b2-bb61-11f1-9d45-91cf9f3cd539/w:1024/p:16x9/AP25243812139636.jpg">© Michael Gonzalez, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Great Black Hope: Pursuit of belonging 'becomes a kind of cancer that eats them from the inside out'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/great-black-hope-pursuit-of-belonging-becomes-a-kind-of-cancer-that-eats-them-from-the-inside-out</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome award-winning author Rob Franklin, joining us to discuss Great Black Hope, his acclaimed debut novel exploring race, class, respectability and belonging. Franklin wanted to write about the worlds he had spent years observing since childhood: including how class and race shape even our most intimate relationships.  At its centre is David Smith, a young Black man from a Southern bourgeois family. His education, manners and connections give him access, but he is constantly aware of the possibility of being cast out. That tension led him to think about respectability politics and the psychological cost of constantly performing an acceptable version of oneself. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202dfae6-bb2c-11f1-9072-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260928-081022-081939-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/202dfae6-bb2c-11f1-9072-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260928-081022-081939-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">258afe08-bb2c-11f1-a8a5-3965a68caf56</guid><pubDate>Mon, 28 Sep 2026 11:37:47 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>The week in pictures: Trump hosts Xi, the pope visits France and floods ravage Thailand</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260927-the-week-in-pictures-trump-hosts-xi-the-pope-visits-france-and-floods-ravage-thailand</link><description>
From Pope Leo XIV's historic first visit to France to US President Donald Trump meeting China's President Xi Jinping to flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">01cd4f8a-b8dd-11f1-9e0d-8725b1555add</guid><pubDate>Sun, 27 Sep 2026 10:05:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3dca1b8c-b999-11f1-8b8a-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/Semaine-Trump-Xi.jpg">© Evan Vucci, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Unusually powerful storm pummels northeast US with heavy rain, high winds</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-unusually-powerful-storm-pummels-northeast-us-with-heavy-rain-high-winds</link><description>
A powerful storm unusual for this time of year intensified on Sunday over the northeastern United States, bringing torrential rain and powerful winds that cut off power to tens of thousands of people and killed one person, according to US media.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f284308-b9ee-11f1-9f6e-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/9a371a7dbd4c6af448fe77d67e88a6972e51d8eb.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f284308-b9ee-11f1-9f6e-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/9a371a7dbd4c6af448fe77d67e88a6972e51d8eb.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">14dcf5fa-b9bc-11f1-85a1-771062ee043c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:08:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5f284308-b9ee-11f1-9f6e-11fa9f8a3b4f/w:1024/p:16x9/9a371a7dbd4c6af448fe77d67e88a6972e51d8eb.jpg">© Joseph Prezioso, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Brazil's President Lula bans online betting ahead of presidential election</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/brazil-s-president-lula-bans-online-betting-ahead-of-presidential-election</link><description>
Brazil’s President Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva on Friday signed an order banning fixed-odds betting just over a week ahead of the first round of the presidential election, in a move he said was designed to tackle the pervasive problem of families falling into debt.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49fe2a58-b9a6-11f1-b2a7-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T010102Z-1209481582-RC2OPNAX5WNZ-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION-LULA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/49fe2a58-b9a6-11f1-b2a7-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-25T010102Z-1209481582-RC2OPNAX5WNZ-RTRMADP-3-BRAZIL-ELECTION-LULA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">459a976a-b9a3-11f1-8cf7-13c445ca7f20</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 12:36:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>CNN removed from Trump press pool despite judge order to reinstate White House access</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260926-cnn-removed-from-trump-press-pool-despite-judge-order-to-reinstate-white-house-access</link><description>
US news outlet CNN has been removed from a press pool that is accompanying President Donald Trump on a trip to Tennessee on Saturday. Last week, the Trump administration barred CNN, along with MS NOW and Politico, from accessing the White House. A judge then ordered their access temporarily restored, saying the move was likely unconstitutional.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1eef422c-b96d-11f1-87e8-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267592547747.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1eef422c-b96d-11f1-87e8-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267592547747.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a1fcd3f4-b96e-11f1-bf02-3df02ebb565c</guid><pubDate>Sat, 26 Sep 2026 05:56:01 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1eef422c-b96d-11f1-87e8-555a0aff87a4/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26267592547747.jpg">©  Alex Brandon, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Lots of pomp but little progress as Trump and Xi end state visit to DC</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-lots-of-pomp-but-no-progress-as-trump-and-xi-end-state-visit</link><description>
US President Donald Trump and Chinese leader Xi Jinping capped a state visit to Washington on Friday with pomp and pageantry but no real breakthroughs. Trump said he discussed the Iran war with Xi during his two-day visit, with both men confirming they will meet twice more before the end of the year.     
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48138eda-b902-11f1-bd61-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/61407f68b9f8f6478e2b8020a9dcf60bd0b6e405.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48138eda-b902-11f1-bd61-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/61407f68b9f8f6478e2b8020a9dcf60bd0b6e405.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">48edc6f4-b902-11f1-a56c-232b84e952df</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:58:08 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/48138eda-b902-11f1-bd61-852b23529bb9/w:1024/p:16x9/61407f68b9f8f6478e2b8020a9dcf60bd0b6e405.jpg">© Saul Loeb, AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>US Supreme Court allows Trump to use controversial voter 'verification' system</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-supreme-court-restores-trump-mass-voter-verification-system-despite-outcry</link><description>
The US Supreme Court on Friday ruled the Trump administration can use a controversial new federal database that would ostensibly verify voter citizenship in November’s elections. Critics argue the administration is exaggerating the threat of non-citizen voters – an extreme rarity in US elections – to implement policies that would disenfranchise likely Democratic voters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477530d0-b8fa-11f1-8e25-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254125465273.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477530d0-b8fa-11f1-8e25-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254125465273.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">6a083630-b8f8-11f1-b50a-a184b40114c3</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 16:52:32 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/477530d0-b8fa-11f1-8e25-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26254125465273.jpg">© Julia Demaree Nikhinson, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump courts Xi Jinping during high-profile White House visit</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-courts-xi-jinping-during-high-profile-white-house-visit</link><description>
President Donald Trump rolled out an unusually lavish welcome for Chinese President Xi Jinping, praising their personal friendship throughout a White House state dinner and other ceremonial events. While both leaders said they held frank discussions behind closed doors, the visit produced no major breakthroughs, prompting criticism from Democratic lawmakers who argued the pageantry overshadowed pressing issues including Iran, Taiwan, AI and trade.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdf9d2e2-b8c2-11f1-bed0-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-081530-081716-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/cdf9d2e2-b8c2-11f1-bed0-8f3418d01115/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260925-081530-081716-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d3a3f2ea-b8c2-11f1-820b-4516fe4dabea</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:38:50 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Argentina's poverty rate climbs to nearly one in three under Milei</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260925-argentina-poverty-rate-nearly-one-in-three-milei</link><description>
Argentina’s poverty rate rose to 32.3% in the first half of 2026 from 28.2% in the previous six months, official data showed on Thursday, as incomes lagged rising prices. Extreme poverty climbed to 7.5% from 6.3%. Among children aged 14 and under, 44.5% were poor.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c52abc8-9aa6-11f1-a07f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26061025634978.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c52abc8-9aa6-11f1-a07f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26061025634978.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a309e418-b887-11f1-8ea3-adbd8b8fbb9d</guid><pubDate>Fri, 25 Sep 2026 02:30:02 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/8c52abc8-9aa6-11f1-a07f-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26061025634978.jpg">© Gustavo Garello, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Truth or Fake</category><title>'Send in the Clowns': Viral video fuels claims Denmark trolled Trump and Rubio</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/send-in-the-clowns-viral-video-fuels-claims-denmark-trolled-trump-and-rubio-1</link><description>
A viral video claims Danish officials played Judy Collins's "Send in the Clowns" as US Secretary of State Marco Rubio arrived for a Greenland signing ceremony, sparking claims of Danish "trolling". Our checks of separate livestreams confirm the song really played and the video was not manipulated. Denmark has denied choosing the music, while the UN says it did not organise the event. Whilst the song was real, there is no evidence Denmark selected it deliberately. Vedika Bahl fact-checks.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25f0245c-b8f4-11f1-bada-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16356352346ab69068ee6893-54589643.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/25f0245c-b8f4-11f1-bada-c959b9d22ec6/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16356352346ab69068ee6893-54589643.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">fb8f2024-b857-11f1-9570-1bd4ffef5edb</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:00:16 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Vedika BAHL</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Israeli policies threaten 'life and existence' of Palestinians, Abbas tells UN</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-israel-policies-threaten-life-existence-palestinian-says-abbas-un</link><description>
Palestinian President Mahmoud Abbas addressed the UN General Assembly on Thursday by video after being denied a visa to the United States for the second year in a row. In his prerecorded speech, he denounced Israeli policies that he said threatened Palestinians with a new Nakba and vowed that his people would remain “on their land”.  
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/737ae326-b82a-11f1-a9cf-a18ad05a0c45/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T142617Z-1582678867-RC2QPNAWN47P-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/737ae326-b82a-11f1-a9cf-a18ad05a0c45/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T142617Z-1582678867-RC2QPNAWN47P-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">00300a1e-b82e-11f1-97a6-1bb92929d4b4</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:54:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/737ae326-b82a-11f1-a9cf-a18ad05a0c45/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-24T142617Z-1582678867-RC2QPNAWN47P-RTRMADP-3-UN-ASSEMBLY.jpg">© Mike Segar, Reuters </source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'Trump views US-China relations as a personal friendship: Xi views US as an adversary to be managed'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/trump-views-us-china-relations-as-a-personal-friendship-xi-views-us-as-an-adversary-to-be-managed</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Henrietta Levin, Senior Fellow with the Freeman Chair in China Studies at the Center for Strategic and International Studies in Washington. The US remains a powerful actor in its relationship with China. But power on paper is not the same thing as leverage at the negotiating table. Levin warns that President Trump’s highly personalized approach to Xi Jinping offers Beijing opportunities that China can easily exploit. Xi does not approach the relationship in the same way. Au contraire, he sees the United States as an adversary to be managed while China pursues its domestic priorities and strategic objectives in Asia, including on Taiwan. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61aec282-b827-11f1-9e10-a18ad05a0c45/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-150401-151641-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/61aec282-b827-11f1-9e10-a18ad05a0c45/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260924-150401-151641-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">67883378-b827-11f1-884b-af4a0164a4c2</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 15:01:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>A propos</category><title>Does the future belong to China?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/a-propos/20260924-does-the-future-belong-to-china</link><description>
US President Donald Trump is rolling out the red carpet for his Chinese counterpart Xi Jinping ahead of Thursday's summit in Washington. But is China's leader overconfident in thinking the future belongs to Beijing? FRANCE 24's Yinka Oyetade speaks to Rex Li from King's College London.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/880eebfa-b80e-11f1-be42-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15234920376ab50f2d4ce053-87492519.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/880eebfa-b80e-11f1-be42-0fb9a8008200/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-15234920376ab50f2d4ce053-87492519.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">68642b70-b80f-11f1-8f79-6ff327f004b8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 12:32:01 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Andrew HILLIAR</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Donald Trump startled by the sound of a fighter jet</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-startled-by-the-sound-of-a-fighter-jet</link><description>
🇺🇸 🇨🇳 As Donald #Trump welcomed his Chinese counterpart Xi #Jinping for a state visit on the tarmac of an airport near #Washington, the sound of a fighter jet during the military ceremony caught the US president off guard, prompting a series of startled facial expressions.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/60a60452-b806-11f1-8b11-6dfe19ed9d2f/w:1024/p:16x9/Xi-00-01-43-22-Still003.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/60a60452-b806-11f1-8b11-6dfe19ed9d2f/w:1024/p:16x9/Xi-00-01-43-22-Still003.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a63295b2-b806-11f1-80b1-35e87443049d</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 11:03:29 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title><![CDATA['Death of the Soccer God' pays 'homage' to Haitian diaspora and 'those who go back & do their best']]></title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/death-of-the-soccer-god-pays-homage-to-haitian-diaspora-and-those-who-go-back-do-their-best</link><description>
Eve Irvine is pleased to welcome Dimitry Elias Léger, journalist and author of "Death of the Soccer God". He begins with an extraordinary but largely forgotten moment in sporting history: the Haitian-born Joe Gaetjens scoring the goal that gave the US its famous victory over England at the 1950 World Cup. But Léger is less interested in reconstructing Gaetjens’s biography than in using the football star's journey as a " jumping point" to examining diaspora, fame, mortality and moral responsibility. Success offers neither immunity from history nor escape from mortality: as he puts it, “You could be super famous and end up on death row” or die wealthy in your own bed: “Either way, you’re going to die.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5087f020-b7e4-11f1-bb89-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16696009676ab4c859433743-47189992.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/5087f020-b7e4-11f1-bb89-cd71256adcef/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-16696009676ab4c859433743-47189992.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b0052c8a-b7de-11f1-80f8-69e474f99f10</guid><pubDate>Thu, 24 Sep 2026 06:29:27 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Americas</category><title>Politico, CNN and MS ​NOW return to White House hours after judge reorders Trump to lift ban</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20260924-us-judge-lifts-trump-s-white-house-ban-on-cnn-ms-now-politico</link><description>
Reporters from ​Politico, CNN and MS ​NOW were allowed to enter the ​White ‌House ⁠on ‌Thursday afternoon after being barred in the morning, despite a US federal judge ordering the reinstatement of their access. The judge then issued a second order for the Trump administration to restore the journalists' access after the media outlets called for an emergency follow-up ⁠hearing. 
